WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.450
Someone once said...

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:59.930
There's baby broccoli with flowers 
made of crunchy, delicious wieners...

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.230
Baby Wiener Broccoli!

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.910
There are ants made out of sweet, sticky,

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.540
soft rice cakes covered with bean jam...

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.180
Be-ant Jam Cakes!

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.250
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.590
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.630
Ichiryu, the president of IGO,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.100
gave Toriko a list of seven 
training ingredients to capture.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.770
The next training ingredient on the list...

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:46.540
...is the Shining Gourami, a 
fish as beautiful as crystal.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:51.040
Shining Gourami dwell in a cavern 
within a certain waterfall,

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.380
Death Falls, also nicknamed Execution Falls.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.050
As might be expected, it's a dangerous place

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.820
that sends whatever comes 
close to its demise.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.650
Sunny was returning home from training

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.190
when Toriko invited him along on the 
trip to capture a Shining Gourami.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.490
What do you think, Sunny?

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:10.800
It's the perfect place to test how far 
you've come in your training, right?

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.970
Certainly, I am interested 
in Shining Gourami.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.710
It may be just the place to 
bathe my new family member,

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.940
who came from the Gourmet World.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.950
The party rode on Sunny's partner, Queen,

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.560
towards the Mors Mountains, 
site of Death Falls!

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:46.530
The Shining Gourami live at the base 
of this mountain, inside Death Falls!

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:54.710
Shocking Rapids! Giant 
Waterfall, Death Falls!

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:25.900
There are more than a thousand rivers 
and lakes in the Mors Mountains.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.740
And this is where they all end up, huh?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:31.910
Does this feel good, Queen?

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.610
Maybe I'll go for a swim, too!

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.420
Komatsu! What do you say we take a dip, too?!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.420
I don't have the energy...

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:45.990
What's wrong?

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.620
"What's wrong?!"

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.930
I was hanging on to Queen for dear life 
while she was moving like a speed demon!

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.860
I never agreed to a roller coaster ride!

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.700
I can't stand thrill 
rides in the first place!

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.500
I'm wiped out...

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.900
But you're not even listening...

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.240
Yeesh...

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.180
This water is so beautiful!

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.410
It's totally clear!

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.020
I can see the bottom of the lake!

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.350
Snow White Sweetfish!

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:27.830
What the...?!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.100
Look at that! What a catch!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.100
You used your hair sensors as a lasso, huh?

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:37.770
I can't see Sunny-san's sensors,

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.670
so it looks like a ton of 
fish floating in the air!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.010
You've really learned how to 
control your hair, even in water!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.050
Shut up! I always had control over it!

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.850
Liar! Before, you couldn't swim a stroke!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.790
Did you practice swimming 
during your training?

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:54.950
Maybe...

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.820
Anyway, what's the difference?

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.030
More importantly, let's eat 
some Snow White Sweetfish!

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.340
I give thanks to all this 
world's great bounty...

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.500
Thank you for the food!

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.010
Delicious!

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.120
Taking naturally caught Snow White Sweetfish

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.790
and adding natural Assalt to make salted 
grilled fish is out of this world!

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.220
What? Assalt, you say?

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.430
You don't know it?!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.860
Um... Here's some.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.130
If you look closely,

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.640
you'll notice that each grain 
of salt is shaped like an ass!

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.640
What kind of foul seasoning is that?!

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:50.170
It's not foul! It's delicious!

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.140
And if only it was called 
"tlassalt", it'd be a palindrome!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.110
That has nothing to do with the taste!

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.620
Come on, you two! Let's 
enjoy eating together!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:06:59.520
Matsu...

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.820
You only emphasize taste, which is why 
you've got such simple sentiments...

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.360
A Stonefish!

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:08.390
It's an ancient fish that's all but extinct!

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:09.990
Would you listen to me?!

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:15.630
At any rate, I wonder why 
this water is so beautiful...

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.540
It's so wondrous that

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:23.710
I find it hard to believe Death 
Falls are really just up ahead.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:29.350
I dove down and it's incredibly clear.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.350
I could see up to about 50 meters.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.850
50 meters?!

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.990
The water is freezing with a 
high degree of calcification

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.230
and its translucence indicates the 
water's total lack of nutritional value.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.290
It has no nutritional value?

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.160
Now that you mention it, there 
aren't many fish in here.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.370
That's because there isn't much plankton.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.300
The sunken but not rotting 
driftwood is proof of that.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.440
There's no bacteria to break it down,

00:07:57.170 --> 00:08:01.040
so the water quality isn't really 
conducive to supporting life.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.450
Where did all the nutrition go?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.710
Over there, Komatsu.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.020
The Mors Mountains function as a filter.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:13.360
All of the nutritional value 
from the huge amount of water

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.620
that runs through the 15,000 
meter-class mountains

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.960
to the river's mouth is 
absorbed by the mountains.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.400
The repository for these nutrients

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:21.800
is none other than

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:25.730
the cavern inside Death Falls 
at the base of the mountains.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:32.770
Then there's a filtrated nutrient-rich 
pool inside the cavern in the waterfall?

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:33.740
Yeah.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:38.150
A pool with a high concentration of all 
the mountains' blessings, so to speak.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:42.620
The fish swimming gracefully there were 
changed by the luminescent energy...

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.650
...into Shining Gourami!

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.460
They really are the chosen fish.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:56.030
Come on, you two, hop on Queen. We're moving.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:08.340
Hey, Sunny.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.280
Before, you said you were going 
to the Road of Three Hells, right?

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.280
You said you were going to meet someone.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.450
And so I did.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:20.250
The Gourmet Gang Leader, Guemon.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.490
He strikes a daunting pose on the road

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.830
that connects the Gourmet 
World and the Human World,

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.390
and sees to it that the Beasts 
from the Gourmet World

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.060
never set foot in the Human World.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.300
I know that sounds nice,

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:37.770
but he really just turned out to be a 
disgusting, vulgar, insensitive old man.

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:40.270
Still, he must have been 
incredibly powerful, right?

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.310
What'd you go see him for, anyway?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.110
To learn a little from his insensitivity.

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:49.680
Insensitivity?

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:52.750
What the hell...?!

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:05.130
W-What the hell is that?!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.170
D-Did a missile or something fall?!

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:12.270
No. It seems we've been given 
our first look at Death Falls.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:16.370
Those are clouds of spray from 
the waterfall's plunge pool.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:17.610
Seriously?!

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:20.610
That's no mere water guillotine...

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.180
It's like a cannon that never stops firing...

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:27.250
Each time with the destructive force 
of a trillion liters of water...

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:29.050
Fascinating!

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:32.060
Go, my Super Spatula...

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.360
Go and test it!

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.560
Let's go, Queen!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.560
Head straight for Death Falls!

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:44.830
Are we really going in there?!

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:47.240
Komatsu! This is training, too!

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:51.470
And since long ago, training by getting 
hit by a waterfall has been a tradition!

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:55.480
The size of <i>this</i> waterfall 
isn't part of any tradition!

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:21.240
T-Toriko-san!

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:22.200
Yeah...

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.020
A-Another one's come!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.620
And it's gigantic!

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:45.660
Yep. Both are as enormous 
as a Regal Mammoth...

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:06.810
This is Execution Falls...

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:08.580
Death Falls!

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:43.480
Let's go home, Toriko-san, Sunny-san...

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:46.750
Watching Death Falls up 
close is impressive...

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:58.560
Huge Beasts like that, gone in an instant!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.070
This is 100% impossible!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.740
Toriko-san, Sunny-san, let's go home!

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:04.970
I see...

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:09.370
Water explosions that contain 
mountain-sized rocks and driftwood...

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:12.040
If it hits you, you won't even know it.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:15.050
So, how should we deal with it?

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.580
How about going underwater?

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:19.980
No good. These two are dead set on going.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:22.520
I don't think water is the way to go.

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:23.120
Look.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:31.800
The plunge pool water is circulating 
violently, creating whirlpools!

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:35.500
The condition of the water is probably 
most akin to a humongous washing machine.

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:39.840
Anything that goes in there will be 
subject to a pulverizing water mixer,

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.840
wiping everything away without a trace.

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:48.950
And yet, the river over the falls is 
all rapids, over 1,000 meters deep.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.680
And since that's running 
down from every side,

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:55.120
we can't proceed by digging through 
rock on one side of the falls either.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.050
Only one thing to do...

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.690
Magnificently, beautifully, 
break through head on...

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:05.700
Sunny!

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:06.160
Sunny-san!

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:17.470
That's surface tension!

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.480
Sunny-san did that before!

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.180
Like a water strider technique!

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.110
Toriko! Matsu!

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.320
I'm pretty sure you guys can't 
do something splendid like this,

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:27.680
so I made this for you!

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:31.450
It's a hair raft made up of my sensors!

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:33.590
Hurry up, get on!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.960
I'll let you ride it just this once!

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:40.630
Of course, without your shoes. 
No wearing shoes on my raft.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.270
Although if you have athlete's 
foot, you better keep 'em on!

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.500
I'm fine barefoot...

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.270
Well done, Sunny!

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.040
Alright! Let's go, Komatsu!

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:51.170
W-W-Wait!

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:56.040
Wait! Toriko-san!!

00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:00.820
Heavy! Toriko, you've gained 
weight, haven't you?!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.020
Have I?

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:05.150
Actually, I think I have been 
putting on more muscle lately...

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.620
Jeez, Toriko-san, could you 
be a little gentler with me?!

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:07.190
It's 'cause I eat nothin' but delicious food!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.790
But since we're on the subject, has 
your hair grown out more recently?

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.990
I mean, if we're going to jump 
down, please warn me first!

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:12.930
It's because I've been training...

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:15.660
I thought my heart would stop! Are 
you listening to me, Toriko-san?!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:16.100
Or to be more precise, the number 
of my sensors has increased.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.630
Right now, I have close to 300,000 strands.

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:22.700
The range of my sensors...

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.670
That is to say, the space 
of my dining kitchen

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.240
has become a maximum of 50 meters.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:30.040
But it's not quantity that's important.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:31.980
It's quality.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:34.610
Queen!

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:47.860
That's...

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:49.860
...a Hippo Shark!

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:54.230
Small fry...

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.640
Two strands should be plenty for him.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:12.280
Super Spatula!

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:29.430
It ate it!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.800
What a jaw! Mother Snake!

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:37.310
Beauty!

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:40.410
You swallowed it whole magnificently, Queen!

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:42.050
That was magnificent?!

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:45.380
Perhaps a swim after your 
meal, for exercise...

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:49.990
We're going to get a little wet 
from that wild water as well.

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:58.400
Okay, let's go.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.000
Let's plunge into Death Falls!

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:08.200
Goggles, Oxygen Leaf, bulletproof suit...

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:12.280
What's all this protective 
equipment for, Toriko-san?

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:15.180
Just get on my back, Komatsu.

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:18.280
Are you sure about Toriko's back, Matsu?

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.980
I could always carry you on my shoulders...

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.750
It's fine! I'll keep Komatsu safe.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.690
We're going inside there.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:31.530
Brace yourself, Toriko.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.370
This waterfall is ginormous!

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.210
So big, I can't tell where it begins or ends!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:48.280
The sound of the water is so 
loud that I can't hear anything!

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.910
It's just as I thought! I can't even breathe!

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.550
This sheet of spray is like a squall...

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:58.690
Komatsu definitely needs that Oxygen Leaf!

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:00.490
Hey! Here it comes!

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.430
Toriko-san! How can the water 
be cutting up your body?!

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.970
When you've got super high 
pressure water flyin' at you,

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:15.700
it's the same as sharp blades!

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:20.810
Cutting metal and glass with 
water pressure is an art form.

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:26.010
By mixing abrasives like grains or 
powder with high pressure water,

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:30.680
it's said that even diamonds, the toughest 
mineral on earth, can be cut through.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:32.590
That's the power of water!

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:35.560
Death Falls also has sand, rocks,

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:39.890
and all kinds of stuff mixed 
in with the high pressure flow!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:43.460
This water's sharpness makes plenty of sense!

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:46.000
And here it comes again!

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:51.770
Fork Shiel...

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:52.740
Quiet, Toriko!

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.910
Hair Lead!

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:04.250
The flow of the water's changed!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:07.550
Dodging a little spray is nothing.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:11.060
I'll lead this wind.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:12.890
That's awesome, Sunny!

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:15.290
Very cool, Sunny-san! Very cool!

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:18.430
Call it beautiful... Beautiful...

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.400
Sunny's sensors are good for everything.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:27.970
But the stress of touching the water 
must be consuming a lot of energy

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.310
and amplifying his fatigue...

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:33.850
So how can he be so composed?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.050
No, not quite composed...

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:40.990
It's more like he's so relaxed that 
he's not thinkin' of anything...

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.920
Hypersensitive Sunny

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:47.230
is controlling his sensors totally 
naturally, like it's nothin'...

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:49.460
Is this a result of his training?

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:52.930
This is what Sunny is now!

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:59.200
Alright! Shall we go in? Into the waterfall!

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.540
Toriko! You help, too!

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:03.640
Of course!

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.480
I'll show you...

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.650
...the result of my training, too!

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:25.360
We give thanks for this food, let's eat!

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:31.230
Yuuuu... Toriko!

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:33.970
Potassium, manganese, calcium, 
starch, fructose, and dextrose

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:36.770
Magnesium, iron, vitamins ABCDE

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:39.640
Vanadium, sodium, glucosamine, chondroitin

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:42.480
Carotintintin, lycopenpenpene, 
isoflavonvonvone

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:45.210
Celery, goya, and green peas

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:48.020
Shiitake, liver, eggplant, bell pepper

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:50.720
What a shame to say "I don't 
even want to look at them!"

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.390
Even if you hate it, gobble 
it down 3 times or 4 times

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.820
and it'll be more and more

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:55.160
Yuuuu... Toriko!

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:57.960
Eat 'em up more! Eat 'em up more!

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.830
More and more and more and 
more and more! Eat 'em all up!

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:05.100
Delicious things are delicious!  
Not even giving them a chance…

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:06.400
Such a waste!

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:09.270
Gobble 'em down more! Gobble 'em down more!

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:12.070
Majorly, deeply, plentifully, 
heartily, gobble 'em down!

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:17.680
They enrich your body and spirit! 
Be grateful to your meals today!

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:20.580
Thanks for the food! All done!

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.850
This week's Gourmet Fortune!

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.460
It's time for Gourmet Fortune, with 
a heaping helping of accuracy!

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:33.060
We're going to use a camera again 
today too, so get yours ready!

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.730
Now then, choose one of these three platters.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:41.270
This week's lucky ingredient 
is in one of them!

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:45.210
The higher the capture level, 
the more Gourmet Luck it has!

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:47.770
Alright, here we go!

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:49.440
A heaping helping...

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:52.510
Open!

00:21:54.150 --> 00:21:55.980
This week's best Gourmet Luck is...

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.390
...yours if you chose B!

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.620
This week, the key to your good fortune

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:04.320
is making full use of your 
ability to take action!

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:08.090
If you chose C, you get this 
week's second-best luck.

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:11.260
Close your eyes when you 
say, "Thanks for the food!"

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:15.030
You'll probably have plenty to eat 
and increase your health luck!

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:18.670
And, I'm sorry. If you chose A, you're third.

00:22:19.010 --> 00:22:20.440
Take care not to waste money.

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:23.840
Treat every gram... I mean, 
every yen as if it's valuable.

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:27.880
Alright, finally it's Gourmet 
Good Luck Charm photo time!

00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:29.380
Are you ready?

00:22:30.050 --> 00:22:34.320
As I announced last week, you-know-who 
is going to put in an appearance!

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:36.290
If you take a photo of that scene

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:39.490
and carry it with you for a week as a 
good luck charm, you'll be even luckier!

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:41.590
Alright, here we go!

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.030
Three! Two! One! Scoop chance!

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.800
The ability to take action! 
Thank you for the food!

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:51.600
Take care not to waste money!

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:55.440
I take action every day!

00:22:56.510 --> 00:22:58.010
That's our Toriko!

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:00.780
Thanks for the photo!

00:23:01.910 --> 00:23:04.820
And now, what you've all been 
waiting for... Check it out!

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:09.050
Time to ride down the raging rapids!

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:11.260
Reach beyond your instincts!

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:13.720
The ultimate hair shreds it's limits!

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:17.090
Sunny's New Attack! the Result of Gorgeous Training!

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:19.070
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
